  "facts": [
    "Fort Pitt Bridge, opened June 19, 1959, was the world’s first computer-designed bowstring arch bridge, weighing 8,066 tons of steel and built for Interstate 376 between the Fort Pitt Tunnel and downtown Pittsburgh.",
    "Designed by George S. Richardson, the bridge’s double‑decked bowstring arch required drivers to navigate a 700‑foot span lane change, especially on the lower level, making it notorious for difficult lane shifts.",
    "The bridge’s ribbon‑cutting ceremony featured Gov. David L. Lawrence, Mayor Thomas Gallagher, and a city fireboat’s hose salute, marking a landmark moment in Pittsburgh’s mid‑century infrastructure boom."
  ],
